Z||000001||loafer87gt||03-04-2001||11:19 PM||||What about the ZR1? When did it come out?||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||03-04-2001||11:26 PM||||I believe (but don't quote me) that the ZR-1 engine (LT-5) was designed/built by Lotus.  Whomever made it, it wasn't the U.S.<P>Is it possible that GM took the LT-5 and used it to help them with the 3.4 TDC?<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||03-04-2001||11:42 PM||||I believe the 3.4L DOHC V6 came out earlier that the ZR-1, which was a V8 by the way. In 1990 Chevrolet introduced the LT5, a technology filled engine developed by Mercury Marine (boat motors) and Lotus. The new design used 4 overhead camshafts and 32 valves, and produced between 375 and 405hp depending on the year. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.exoticmuscle.com/vette/engine/engine-LT5.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.exoticmuscle.com/vette/engine/engine-LT5.htm</A>   <P>Of course, Cadillac now has the NorthStar 32-valve DOHC V8 engine.<P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 03-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||03-05-2001||12:11 AM||||I know the ZR-1 is a V-8.......I was just thinking that they used the 4 valve per cyl. technology learned from that motor to help develop the 3.4 TDC (also w/4 valves per cyl).<P>The ZR-1 was introduced in 1989 as a 1990 model (they made the ZR-1 through 1995).<P>I don't think the 3.4 TDC came out until 1992, so the LT-5 was around first.  <P>I knew Lotus had a hand in the development of the LT-5, but I couldn't remember who else was involved.....thanks for reminding me about Mercury Marine.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||03-05-2001||01:00 AM||||Also, don't forget the 225 HP SOHC Pontiac Sprint 6! My buddy had a Firebird with one of those and it was a peppy little engine ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||03-05-2001||01:24 AM||||The 3.4 TDC came out in '91, using mostly technology from the quad 4.  It was desinged to be the quad's "big brother".||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wannabe||03-05-2001||08:02 AM||||1974 Cosworth Vega...4 cyl 16 valve 145 hp 2.3l, all aluminum engine...pretty good for a domestic 4 cyl back then. Supposedly, the TDC V6 was developed from the Quad 4.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||03-05-2001||10:28 AM||||What I really like about the TDC is that it is a factory DOHC conversion on a block that is almost the same as the pushrod block.<P>Oh yeah... For enough money, Lingenfelter will punch your LT5 out to 415 cubic inches and around 600 HP.<p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 03-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||LottaBallsCamaro||03-05-2001||10:54 PM||||The 3.4TDC was the first V6 dohc. The LT5 is the engine that went into the ZR1.<P>------------------<BR>91'RS 305TBI no mods to date<BR>92' Lumina 275,000 miles and still humping!!!!||||reg||1
